  "paragraph": 32,
  "text": "With traces in hand, benchmark harness changes like real systems engineering instead of vibes. Run a fixed suite of realistic repository tasks and separate capability ceiling from production consistency. Pass at K asks whether the agent solved a task at least once in K attempts. Pass to the K asks whether it succeeded on all K runs in a row. An eighty percent single-run agent looks great on pass at three, yet drops to fifty-one percent on pass to the third. Track that reliability curve alongside cost per solved task and median turns.",
